WEBVTT

00:01:20.906 --> 00:01:24.344
&lt;i&gt;theCerritos is
beginning a 12-hour warp,&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:24.388 --> 00:01:27.652
&lt;i&gt;en route to a planetary survey
in the Kontaran system.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:27.695 --> 00:01:30.220
&lt;i&gt;With little to do
in this vacant stretch of space,&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:30.263 --> 00:01:33.745
&lt;i&gt;I've approved some much needed
R and R for the crew.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:36.226 --> 00:01:38.053
I can't believe
we all have the day off.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.794
What should we do?
Strategema tournament?

00:01:39.838 --> 00:01:41.318
Oh, I can't. Dr. T'Ana

00:01:41.361 --> 00:01:42.884
invited me to a thing
on the holodeck.

00:01:42.928 --> 00:01:44.538
I really need to get
on her good side.

00:01:44.582 --> 00:01:45.800
I can't tell if she likes me

00:01:45.844 --> 00:01:46.845
or if she makes that face
at everyone.

00:01:46.888 --> 00:01:48.542
Oh, okay. Uh, Rutherford?

00:01:48.586 --> 00:01:51.110
Hey, sorry, Billups has
a new soup recipe he asked me

00:01:51.154 --> 00:01:53.504
to try out and,
after that, I promised Shaxs

00:01:53.547 --> 00:01:54.983
I'd throw some pottery with him.

00:01:55.027 --> 00:01:56.898
Jeez, what is this,
commander hangout day?

00:01:56.942 --> 00:01:58.726
Huh, guess it's just me and you.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:00.902
I'm "with the captain" today.

00:02:00.946 --> 00:02:02.774
- What do you mean?
- Oh, she's been bugging me to do

00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:04.863
some mother/daughter stuff,
and I've been putting it off

00:02:04.906 --> 00:02:06.517
forever, and now
with this long haul,

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.083
she knows I've got no excuse.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:09.911
All you guys are spending warp
with a bridge buddy?

00:02:09.955 --> 00:02:11.261
It's not a big deal.

00:02:11.304 --> 00:02:12.740
Uh, yes, it is!

00:02:12.784 --> 00:02:14.177
Socializing with a commander can be

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.787
a huge factor
in getting a promotion.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.876
Well, you've got 12 hours,
why don't you rub some elbows

00:02:17.919 --> 00:02:19.007
and make a new friend?

00:02:19.051 --> 00:02:20.444
I wish I served on a ship

00:02:20.487 --> 00:02:22.097
that had built-in
social structures,

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:23.838
like with Binars or Klingons.

00:02:23.882 --> 00:02:25.231
Um, have you ever been
on a Klingon ship?

00:02:25.275 --> 00:02:27.059
I don't think you'd like it.

00:02:27.102 --> 00:02:28.887
They've been
warping around the quadrant

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.845
for centuries.
I bet their Lower Decks are

00:02:30.889 --> 00:02:32.804
a lot nicer than you'd think.

00:02:44.729 --> 00:02:46.252
- Come, M'ach.

00:02:46.296 --> 00:02:48.689
Let us eat before
the squirmiest &lt;i&gt;gagh&lt;/i&gt; is devoured.

00:02:48.733 --> 00:02:50.256
Do not speak of &lt;i&gt;gagh.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.302
Today I am tasked
with scraping out

00:02:52.345 --> 00:02:55.609
the worm barrels and
replenishing their blood supply.

00:02:55.653 --> 00:02:57.263
That is the worst.

00:02:57.307 --> 00:02:59.222
I have combat training all day.

00:02:59.265 --> 00:03:01.615
Save me a seat at lunch,
unless I die an honorable death,

00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:03.138
then someone else can have it.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.924
Today will be
a day of great honor for me.

00:03:05.967 --> 00:03:07.795
I am filling in at the helm.

00:03:07.839 --> 00:03:09.580
Yes, the honor is palpable.

00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:11.799
Have you not noticed
that Commander Togg

00:03:11.843 --> 00:03:13.758
has been undermining
the captain?

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.281
If so, then he should be killed.

00:03:15.325 --> 00:03:18.066
Exactly, and stationed
at the captain's side,

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:19.807
I will be the logical choice

00:03:19.851 --> 00:03:21.635
to be the new first officer.

00:03:21.679 --> 00:03:23.768
-"Logical"?

00:03:23.811 --> 00:03:25.422
Are you a Vulcan now?

00:03:25.465 --> 00:03:28.120
Maybe you should trim your bangs
and join a science vessel.

00:03:30.078 --> 00:03:32.994
Could you imagine serving
with those &lt;i&gt;biHnuchs?&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:33.038 --> 00:03:34.953
"Avoid death, and cower."

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.185
Would anyone care
for a game of chess

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.536
when we are finished
with our second duty shift?

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:55.843
No. I will be composing
an arrangement for the lute,

00:03:55.887 --> 00:03:58.019
which should take several hours.

00:03:58.063 --> 00:04:00.283
I am available for chess.

00:04:00.326 --> 00:04:01.936
- Hmm.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.983
I have detected an anomalous
surge of metreon particles

00:04:05.026 --> 00:04:08.160
in System 7743.8.

00:04:08.203 --> 00:04:11.685
System 7743.8 is beyond
our scanning range.

00:04:11.729 --> 00:04:14.166
It would be, but I have
implemented personal algorithms,

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:16.342
which increase
our long range sensors.

00:04:16.386 --> 00:04:17.865
T'Lyn.

00:04:17.909 --> 00:04:21.260
Your assignment was to monitor
tertiary impulse systems.

00:04:21.304 --> 00:04:23.001
That is a redundant system.

00:04:23.044 --> 00:04:24.437
I wanted to...

00:04:24.481 --> 00:04:27.048
It is logical to improve
our scanning capabilities,

00:04:27.092 --> 00:04:29.224
instead of observing
non-essential systems.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:31.705
These readings are
within acceptable parameters.

00:04:31.749 --> 00:04:34.404
Correct. However, this region
has never produced this type

00:04:34.447 --> 00:04:37.232
of anomalous energy.
Does that not seem... strange?

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:40.061
Anomalies, by definition,
are strange.

00:04:40.105 --> 00:04:41.585
Something about this feels off.

00:04:41.628 --> 00:04:43.064
"Feels off"?

00:04:43.108 --> 00:04:45.415
You have been spoken to
about this before, T'Lyn.

00:04:45.458 --> 00:04:46.981
It is illogical
to ignore something

00:04:47.025 --> 00:04:48.635
of statistical significance.

00:04:48.679 --> 00:04:51.421
I must inform the captain.

00:04:52.247 --> 00:04:54.685
She has lost all control.

00:04:58.428 --> 00:05:00.691
Today is a good day to be a--

00:05:02.214 --> 00:05:04.738
It is you who is dishonorable!

00:05:04.782 --> 00:05:06.914
You dare spit lies on my ship?!

00:05:10.048 --> 00:05:11.441
Coward! You hide behind

00:05:11.484 --> 00:05:13.834
- the name of--
- I hide behind nothing!

00:05:18.622 --> 00:05:21.276
Togg forgot what it means
to be Klingon.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.366
I need a loyal first officer,

00:05:23.409 --> 00:05:27.282
a soldier of the empire who does
not spit in the face of duty.

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.110
The job will go to whoever

00:05:29.154 --> 00:05:31.286
impresses me most today.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.636
Remove this.

00:05:32.679 --> 00:05:36.030
I don't want that stench
on my bridge.

00:05:36.074 --> 00:05:38.206
I will take care of it, Captain.

00:05:48.478 --> 00:05:51.437
Okay, let's snag a bridge buddy.

00:05:51.481 --> 00:05:53.657
"Kimarnt, her head cloudy"?

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.441
Ah, thank you, Ensign...

00:05:55.485 --> 00:05:57.661
Boimler. I took a little
Tamarian at the Academy.

00:05:57.704 --> 00:06:00.751
Ah, "Unzak and Vhila
as children?"

00:06:00.794 --> 00:06:02.492
Oh, uh, right, um--

00:06:02.535 --> 00:06:05.625
"Karno, in the forest
with... Mira."

00:06:05.669 --> 00:06:08.062
It is hard to lose weight

00:06:08.106 --> 00:06:10.021
when you can replicate
any food you want!

00:06:10.064 --> 00:06:11.936
No, no, no,
that's not what I meant!

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:14.547
Dang it!

00:06:18.638 --> 00:06:21.989
Aw, hey, Boimler. I didn't know
you had a passion for pottery.

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:23.338
Uh, Kayshon and I didn't
really mesh.

00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:24.818
Since you have
two bridge buddies,

00:06:24.862 --> 00:06:25.993
I thought we could share?

00:06:26.037 --> 00:06:27.342
Okie dokie!

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.388
Take your never-ending
bonfire of rage

00:06:29.432 --> 00:06:31.129
and bury it in the clay.

00:06:31.172 --> 00:06:32.609
Get out of here, rage!

00:06:32.652 --> 00:06:34.915
That's a neat pot,
Lieutenant Shaxs-- did you learn

00:06:34.959 --> 00:06:36.656
how to do that back on Bajor?

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.789
What did you just say?

00:06:38.832 --> 00:06:41.356
I just asked if you learned
how to throw pots on Bajor.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.402
- No, no, no, no, no.
- Oh, do we not talk about Bajor?

00:06:43.446 --> 00:06:45.230
You think I had time

00:06:45.273 --> 00:06:46.492
for anything
other than resisting?!

00:06:46.536 --> 00:06:49.190
Fighting fascism
is a full-time job!

00:06:49.234 --> 00:06:51.192
- Run! He's not kidding!
- Aah!

00:06:52.716 --> 00:06:54.761
Put it in the clay, Papa Bear.
Put it in the clay.

00:06:54.805 --> 00:06:56.284
I'm going to fight.

00:06:56.328 --> 00:06:58.504
I'm going to get revenge. I'm...

00:06:58.548 --> 00:07:00.811
going to a make
a cute little ashtray

00:07:00.854 --> 00:07:02.465
for my incense.

00:07:02.508 --> 00:07:04.597
It's going to look like a puppy.

00:07:04.641 --> 00:07:06.556
Ooh, a puppy.

00:07:10.951 --> 00:07:12.866
Yes!

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.259
Good boy!

00:07:14.302 --> 00:07:16.914
That is what we will do
to enemy &lt;i&gt;petaQs.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:18.959 --> 00:07:20.352
Drink to honor!

00:07:20.395 --> 00:07:23.224
Captain, your targ is
most impressive.

00:07:23.268 --> 00:07:24.530
Like Kor's hound

00:07:24.574 --> 00:07:26.401
at the Battle
of Klach D'kel Brakt.

00:07:26.445 --> 00:07:28.447
Oh, I'm surprised
someone your age

00:07:28.491 --> 00:07:30.405
knows of that glorious day.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.277
Oh, it is one
of my favorite slaughters.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.671
We could sing
a song about it, if--

00:07:36.063 --> 00:07:39.023
The blood wine barrel
runs low-- fetch us more.

00:07:39.066 --> 00:07:41.504
- Yes, sir.

00:07:43.854 --> 00:07:47.422
Why would you modify already
adequate long-range sensors,

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:49.512
when that is outside
of your duties?

00:07:49.555 --> 00:07:51.296
I had a gut feeling
that increasing

00:07:51.339 --> 00:07:52.950
our sensor range
may prove illuminating.

00:07:52.993 --> 00:07:55.735
And now you want to adjust
our current heading

00:07:55.779 --> 00:07:58.564
by 1.7 degrees,
because of this...

00:07:58.608 --> 00:07:59.652
"instinct."

00:07:59.696 --> 00:08:01.436
The energy originated
in a region

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:04.048
which has never experienced
a comparable phenomenon.

00:08:04.091 --> 00:08:06.311
To ignore it would be illogical.

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:11.316
Helm, adjust course
to 577 mark 6.

00:08:11.359 --> 00:08:13.884
Do not take my action
as an endorsement

00:08:13.927 --> 00:08:15.363
of your behavior.

00:08:15.407 --> 00:08:17.365
You will spend the next two days
in meditation.

00:08:17.409 --> 00:08:18.932
No, I do not have time for that.

00:08:18.976 --> 00:08:21.195
I have another project,
which is nearing culmination.

00:08:21.239 --> 00:08:22.588
T'Lyn, get ahold of yourself.

00:08:22.632 --> 00:08:24.547
These outbursts will not be
tolerated.

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.940
work on your self-control.

00:08:26.984 --> 00:08:28.594
Through silent meditation.

00:08:28.638 --> 00:08:31.118
- Captain, I believe that
I could modify the--
- Beliefs,

00:08:31.162 --> 00:08:32.555
feelings, instincts.

00:08:32.598 --> 00:08:34.818
You are behaving like a child.

00:08:40.824 --> 00:08:42.173
You were right, Dr. T.

00:08:42.216 --> 00:08:43.696
This is amazing!

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:46.090
Ah, nothing like clawing
your way up the side

00:08:46.133 --> 00:08:48.614
of a giant, hard piece
of earth to feel alive.

00:08:48.658 --> 00:08:51.617
Boimler!
What are you doing up here?

00:08:51.661 --> 00:08:53.750
Just wanted to catch up
in the old hover boots and see

00:08:53.793 --> 00:08:56.404
if you guys needed a climbing
partner-- Hi, Dr. T'Ana.

00:08:56.448 --> 00:08:58.102
You didn't bring any gear?

00:08:58.145 --> 00:09:00.626
Well, uh, I-I-I have the shirt
and, uh, you know, the boots.

00:09:04.804 --> 00:09:06.371
Good thing safety protocols
are on.

00:09:06.414 --> 00:09:08.242
They-they are on, right?

00:09:08.286 --> 00:09:10.462
I don't know. Sure.

00:09:10.505 --> 00:09:13.204
Ow, ow, ow!

00:09:19.514 --> 00:09:21.516
Hmm.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.518
Why would you tell
an entire shift

00:09:23.562 --> 00:09:25.303
I get bad cramps?!

00:09:25.346 --> 00:09:27.087
You were on duty!

00:09:27.131 --> 00:09:29.612
Your commanding officers have
to know any medical issues

00:09:29.655 --> 00:09:31.396
that could impact the mission!

00:09:31.439 --> 00:09:33.006
Billups doesn't need to know!

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.356
He's not good with that stuff,
it freaked him out!

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.315
If I had to dance around
everything that freaks out

00:09:37.358 --> 00:09:39.012
Billups, we wouldn't get
anything done!

00:09:39.056 --> 00:09:41.624
Cool! Then maybe I'll tell him
to boost the environmental

00:09:41.667 --> 00:09:43.887
controls to help
with your hot flashes!

00:09:50.633 --> 00:09:53.505
Oh, nothing
like that Hawaiian surf.

00:09:53.548 --> 00:09:55.072
Crisp air, tasty waves.

00:09:55.115 --> 00:09:57.074
- This is gonna be great.
- Sir.

00:09:57.117 --> 00:10:00.338
Ensign. Oh, you remember
those luaus, on the beach?

00:10:00.381 --> 00:10:02.557
- Ah, so good!
- Yeah, friggin' pigs, dude!

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:04.559
Nothing like the feel
of Hawaiian sand

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:06.649
after riding
those tropical waves.

00:10:06.692 --> 00:10:09.695
Mr. Boimler,
are you also from Hawaii?

00:10:09.739 --> 00:10:11.871
From-from Hawaii? Oh, uh...

00:10:11.915 --> 00:10:14.439
He has to be-- only people
who grew up on the islands

00:10:14.482 --> 00:10:16.397
like us could describe it
like that.

00:10:16.441 --> 00:10:18.008
You're all from Hawaii?

00:10:18.051 --> 00:10:19.400
Um, aloha!

00:10:19.444 --> 00:10:20.837
Yep, small galaxy, huh?

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:23.317
I can't believe there's
another Hawaiian onboard!

00:10:23.361 --> 00:10:24.928
We're hitting the beach
this afternoon.

00:10:24.971 --> 00:10:27.060
Holodeck Three--
you should join us.

00:10:27.104 --> 00:10:28.714
To clean up or...

00:10:28.758 --> 00:10:30.803
No, to hang out!

00:10:30.847 --> 00:10:32.718
Unless you don't miss
the islands?

00:10:32.762 --> 00:10:35.503
No, I mean, yeah, I mean,
I am homesick for Hawaii.

00:10:35.547 --> 00:10:38.332
I grew up in Hawaii
and, man, do I miss Hawaii.

00:10:38.376 --> 00:10:41.248
- Wait, didn't you say
you're from a vineyard?
- Uh...

00:10:41.292 --> 00:10:43.468
- Pineapple or coffee?
- Both?

00:10:43.511 --> 00:10:46.689
Whoa! Now that's tropical.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:53.783
Next time, fetch your own wine.

00:10:57.438 --> 00:10:58.918
I demand assistance.

00:10:58.962 --> 00:11:01.051
Could someone just--

00:11:01.094 --> 00:11:03.314
Captain, ah, yes, I thank you.

00:11:03.357 --> 00:11:05.098
I cannot move this overweight...

00:11:05.142 --> 00:11:07.448
When you're done
fooling around, walk my targ.

00:11:07.492 --> 00:11:10.277
He ate that traitor's leg, and
will need to be shuffled around

00:11:10.321 --> 00:11:12.976
until it passes,
or he will have gas.

00:11:13.933 --> 00:11:16.022
Yes, sir.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.427
You are working
instead of meditating.

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:30.950
I am nearly finished.
I will meditate

00:11:30.994 --> 00:11:32.647
as soon
as the project is complete.

00:11:32.691 --> 00:11:34.258
You know
your rebellions will only

00:11:34.301 --> 00:11:35.694
lead to punitive spiritualism.

00:11:35.738 --> 00:11:37.348
I am not rebellious.

00:11:37.391 --> 00:11:40.481
I simply am enjoying the project
and hoped to finish it today

00:11:40.525 --> 00:11:42.483
so I can continue
with other work.

00:11:42.527 --> 00:11:44.659
Perhaps if you did not
spend all of your time

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:46.792
following rules,
you, too, would appreciate

00:11:46.836 --> 00:11:49.316
that there is more for us
to learn and achieve.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.014
Are you attempting to insult me?

00:11:51.057 --> 00:11:52.972
I merely wish for you
to join me in broadening

00:11:53.016 --> 00:11:54.931
your definition of how
to synthesize data.

00:11:54.974 --> 00:11:56.802
That sounds
like an insult to me.

00:11:56.846 --> 00:11:59.109
Perhaps you could look to me
as your confidant.

00:11:59.152 --> 00:12:01.241
In Klingon culture,
they designate those who stand

00:12:01.285 --> 00:12:02.677
with one another as &lt;i&gt;cha'DIch.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:02.721 --> 00:12:04.331
We are not Klingon.

00:12:04.375 --> 00:12:05.811
Nor are we Borg drones.

00:12:05.855 --> 00:12:07.813
We do not have
to blindly follow orders.

00:12:07.857 --> 00:12:10.729
"Logic is the beginning
of wisdom, not the end."

00:12:10.773 --> 00:12:13.166
The high command would be
most interested to learn

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.994
of your relaxed attitude.

00:12:15.038 --> 00:12:17.170
How would they find out?
Would you report me?

00:12:17.214 --> 00:12:20.173
If it is for your own good.
You are clearly unstable.

00:12:20.217 --> 00:12:22.132
You are not yourself, T'Lyn.

00:12:22.175 --> 00:12:24.525
- Everyone has noticed.
- Then I hope they notice

00:12:24.569 --> 00:12:27.137
how unconcerned I am
about their assessment.

00:12:28.965 --> 00:12:31.532
Why didn't you just tell them
you're not from Hawaii?

00:12:31.576 --> 00:12:33.665
I tried! Sort of.
It all just happened fast!

00:12:33.708 --> 00:12:35.536
Suddenly I was just part
of the &lt;i&gt;ohana.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.278
- Isn't that what you wanted?
- Yeah, but what if Ransom
finds out I lied?

00:12:38.322 --> 00:12:40.193
He could demote me to work
at a penal colony where

00:12:40.237 --> 00:12:42.935
I'd have to mate with the enemy
to form a new civilization...

00:12:42.979 --> 00:12:45.372
&lt;i&gt;Ensign Mariner, report
to my quarters for hanging out.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:46.896 --> 00:12:50.203
This is the longest warp
of my life!

00:12:54.077 --> 00:12:55.382
I don't know, Boimler.

00:12:55.426 --> 00:12:56.862
I think you should
just come clean.

00:12:56.906 --> 00:12:58.342
Yeah, I mean what's really

00:12:58.385 --> 00:13:01.127
having a commander friend
or being true to yourself?

00:13:01.171 --> 00:13:03.869
Yeah, yeah. You're right.

00:13:03.913 --> 00:13:06.393
Aloha!

00:13:06.437 --> 00:13:08.700
Hey, hey! Aloha!

00:13:24.368 --> 00:13:26.239
Captain,
the leg has been passed.

00:13:26.283 --> 00:13:27.675
It was an honorable movement.

00:13:27.719 --> 00:13:30.548
The empire used
to choke the quadrant

00:13:30.591 --> 00:13:33.507
with fear, power, but now?

00:13:33.551 --> 00:13:35.248
We've lost our way.

00:13:35.292 --> 00:13:36.902
The empire still strikes terror.

00:13:36.946 --> 00:13:39.600
Klingon blood runs
as reddish-pink as ever.

00:13:39.644 --> 00:13:41.298
Klingons joining Starfleet.

00:13:41.341 --> 00:13:43.169
Studying at Bajoran academies.

00:13:43.213 --> 00:13:45.128
No hunger for victory.

00:13:45.171 --> 00:13:46.912
No respect for tradition.

00:13:46.956 --> 00:13:49.175
It is troubling to see
a proud caste of warriors

00:13:49.219 --> 00:13:51.090
lose their &lt;i&gt;lurDech.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:51.134 --> 00:13:52.831
Well put.

00:13:52.875 --> 00:13:55.529
You are a true Klingon.

00:13:55.573 --> 00:13:57.662
You may be smaller and weaker

00:13:57.705 --> 00:14:00.273
and slower and smaller
than my other officers.

00:14:00.317 --> 00:14:02.058
But you have a warrior's spirit.

00:14:02.101 --> 00:14:05.278
One day, you could be
captain of your own ship.

00:14:05.322 --> 00:14:07.585
That would be
my greatest honor, sir.

00:14:07.628 --> 00:14:09.195
Uh, besides dying in battle.

00:14:09.239 --> 00:14:11.981
&lt;i&gt;That&lt;/i&gt; would be
my greatest-greatest honor.

00:14:12.024 --> 00:14:13.591
&lt;i&gt;Captain, we're being hailed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:13.634 --> 00:14:15.332
Put it in my quarters.
Private channel.

00:14:15.375 --> 00:14:17.551
- Pakled!
- Oh, hi.

00:14:17.595 --> 00:14:19.814
Are you ready
to give us presents?

00:14:19.858 --> 00:14:22.208
We will discuss
our transaction in person.

00:14:22.252 --> 00:14:24.297
I'm beaming over with my new

00:14:24.341 --> 00:14:25.646
second-in-command.

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:27.387
Thank you, Captain.

00:14:27.431 --> 00:14:29.824
Pah, Pakleds have no honor.

00:14:29.868 --> 00:14:31.914
Are we commandeering their ship?

00:14:31.957 --> 00:14:35.439
Even cowards
and fools have their uses.

00:14:35.482 --> 00:14:36.962
I do not understand.

00:14:37.006 --> 00:14:39.182
Pakleds have
an insatiable hunger for power.

00:14:39.225 --> 00:14:40.792
I can use that.

00:14:40.835 --> 00:14:42.750
With the weapons and information
I've armed them with,

00:14:42.794 --> 00:14:45.449
they've thrown the entire
quadrant into discord.

00:14:45.492 --> 00:14:47.103
You are helping them?

00:14:47.146 --> 00:14:49.061
With the Federation
destabilized,

00:14:49.105 --> 00:14:51.716
the empire can claim
the region as our own.

00:14:51.759 --> 00:14:54.153
Our greatest day is yet to come.

00:14:54.197 --> 00:14:56.982
Klingons do not allow someone
else to fight our battles.

00:14:57.026 --> 00:14:59.898
Which is exactly
why the Federation

00:14:59.942 --> 00:15:02.727
has no idea
who is manipulating them.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:07.079
"Cry havoc
and let slip the dogs of war."

00:15:10.213 --> 00:15:11.562
I think it was the chef,

00:15:11.605 --> 00:15:12.998
in the bio lab,
with a sniper rifle

00:15:13.042 --> 00:15:14.347
that can shoot through walls.

00:15:14.391 --> 00:15:16.132
You always pick the chef.

00:15:16.175 --> 00:15:17.698
Yeah, 'cause we have
replicators.

00:15:17.742 --> 00:15:19.004
Why is there a chef?
That's just shady.

00:15:19.048 --> 00:15:20.658
&lt;i&gt;Captain, we've picked up&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:20.701 --> 00:15:22.094
&lt;i&gt;an anomalous
energy reading nearby.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:22.138 --> 00:15:23.530
&lt;i&gt;Should we drop out of warp
and investigate?&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:23.574 --> 00:15:24.836
- Yes!
- Yes, please!

00:15:24.879 --> 00:15:26.533
All right,
let's get back to work.

00:15:26.577 --> 00:15:28.361
Ooh, I cannot believe
I'm saying that.

00:15:28.405 --> 00:15:30.189
- Mariner.
- What? I know.

00:15:30.233 --> 00:15:32.191
I don't care
who the fake killer was.

00:15:32.235 --> 00:15:34.367
I had a good time today.

00:15:34.411 --> 00:15:36.021
I know.

00:15:36.065 --> 00:15:37.631
I did, too.

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:45.378
Welcome to the Pakled
spaceship, &lt;i&gt;Pakled.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:45.422 --> 00:15:46.814
I am Rebner.

00:15:46.858 --> 00:15:49.295
Ah, yes, Rebner,
we've met several times.

00:15:49.339 --> 00:15:50.731
We need another boomer.

00:15:50.775 --> 00:15:53.212
What? No, one Varuvian bomb
is enough.

00:15:53.256 --> 00:15:54.561
We already used it.

00:15:54.605 --> 00:15:56.302
You used it?! On what? Why?

00:15:56.346 --> 00:15:58.696
We wanted to test it
on a big asteroid,

00:15:58.739 --> 00:16:00.785
but then it stopped working.

00:16:00.828 --> 00:16:02.482
It was a bomb!

00:16:02.526 --> 00:16:04.136
You can only use it once!

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:06.834
This is Dorg.
Transport another explosive

00:16:06.878 --> 00:16:08.575
- onto the Pakled vessel. &lt;i&gt;
- Yes, Captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:08.619 --> 00:16:11.752
Captain, a Varuvian explosion
would emit metreon particles.

00:16:11.796 --> 00:16:13.928
- Other ships may come
to investigate.

00:16:13.972 --> 00:16:16.148
&lt;i&gt;Red alarm. Red alarm.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:23.677 --> 00:16:25.418
Damn it!
Block their communications!

00:16:25.462 --> 00:16:27.942
We have to take out that ship!

00:16:27.986 --> 00:16:29.901
What the-- The Pakleds again?

00:16:29.944 --> 00:16:31.424
And now
they're threatening Klingons?

00:16:31.468 --> 00:16:32.773
Hail the Bird-of-Prey.

00:16:32.817 --> 00:16:34.253
No response, Captain.

00:16:34.297 --> 00:16:35.428
Klingon ship, this is

00:16:35.472 --> 00:16:37.082
the Federation
Starship &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:37.126 --> 00:16:38.779
We've dealt with Pakleds before.

00:16:38.823 --> 00:16:40.781
Are you in need of aid?

00:16:42.392 --> 00:16:44.655
Captain, both vessels
are powering weapons.

00:16:44.698 --> 00:16:46.787
What?! Shields up! Red alert!

00:16:50.095 --> 00:16:52.663
- Dude, my Mai Tai.

00:16:52.706 --> 00:16:54.447
Hawaiianers,
we're under attack!

00:17:03.674 --> 00:17:06.155
Target their weapons!

00:17:07.069 --> 00:17:09.245
- Shields holding at 80%.

00:17:12.422 --> 00:17:14.337
Return fire! Full spread!

00:17:16.165 --> 00:17:18.297
Deck Six is taking heavy damage.

00:17:18.341 --> 00:17:19.429
Sealing the area.

00:17:19.472 --> 00:17:21.779
Damn it!
We have to get to the bridge!

00:17:21.822 --> 00:17:23.868
I don't want to die
in a Hawaiian shirt.

00:17:24.782 --> 00:17:27.219
I'm not from Hawaii.

00:17:27.263 --> 00:17:28.655
And if I don't make it
through this,

00:17:28.699 --> 00:17:29.961
I don't want to die a liar.

00:17:30.004 --> 00:17:31.702
Sir, I'm from Modesto,
California.

00:17:31.745 --> 00:17:33.356
I just wanted
to find a bridge buddy.

00:17:33.399 --> 00:17:34.661
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:34.705 --> 00:17:37.360
I'm not from Hawaii, either.

00:17:37.403 --> 00:17:40.841
I never felt like I belonged,
until I met the rest of you.

00:17:40.885 --> 00:17:42.408
Neither am I. None of us are.

00:17:42.452 --> 00:17:44.062
We just wanted to be friends
with you, sir.

00:17:44.106 --> 00:17:46.151
You guys didn't have to pretend

00:17:46.195 --> 00:17:48.849
to be something you aren't.
I like you for you.

00:17:48.893 --> 00:17:50.199
Really? Thanks, Commander.

00:17:50.242 --> 00:17:52.897
- Also, I'm not from Hawaii.
- Wait, what now?

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:54.290
I made it up
when I was an ensign

00:17:54.333 --> 00:17:56.553
and my commanding officer
was from Honolulu.

00:17:56.596 --> 00:17:58.903
I'm actually from the Moon.

00:17:58.946 --> 00:18:00.600
Wait, bro, Earth's moon?

00:18:00.644 --> 00:18:02.602
That's where I'm from! Luna Bay!

00:18:02.646 --> 00:18:05.214
- Tyco City!
- My sister went
to Tyco City Prep!

00:18:05.257 --> 00:18:07.172
I'm from
the Third Moon of Benzar!

00:18:07.216 --> 00:18:09.348
B-9-3? That's a great moon!

00:18:09.392 --> 00:18:10.741
My cousin lives there!

00:18:10.784 --> 00:18:12.177
We're all moon buddies?

00:18:12.221 --> 00:18:14.179
You know, some people say
Modesto is like the moon

00:18:14.223 --> 00:18:16.877
of, uh, San Francisco,
so I guess I'm from a moon, too.

00:18:16.921 --> 00:18:18.923
Modesto is not a moon.

00:18:18.966 --> 00:18:20.838
If you were from a moon,
you'd know

00:18:20.881 --> 00:18:22.492
how deeply insulting that is.

00:18:22.535 --> 00:18:24.407
What? You guys pretended
to be from Hawaii!

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.365
- That's like the most
culturally insensitive--

00:18:28.454 --> 00:18:30.630
Let the Pakleds take
the final shot.

00:18:30.674 --> 00:18:32.676
They're about to start a war.

00:18:32.719 --> 00:18:34.199
This feels wrong.
There is no honor

00:18:34.243 --> 00:18:36.593
in letting others fight
our battles.

00:18:36.636 --> 00:18:38.377
Do not talk to me of honor!

00:18:38.421 --> 00:18:40.597
I have been crushing &lt;i&gt;baktags
beneath my boot&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:43.208
since before you were born!

00:18:43.252 --> 00:18:46.733
Other Klingons have tried
to sabotage peace before.

00:18:46.777 --> 00:18:49.214
- They failed.
- I will not.

00:18:49.258 --> 00:18:52.435
They will write songs of me
this day!

00:19:00.138 --> 00:19:03.533
&lt;i&gt;Red alarm! Red alarm! Red alarm!&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:03.576 --> 00:19:05.622
I am hungry.

00:19:05.665 --> 00:19:07.319
You should eat.

00:19:07.363 --> 00:19:08.842
You are smart.

00:19:08.886 --> 00:19:10.366
&lt;i&gt;Red alarm!&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:10.409 --> 00:19:12.281
Evasive maneuvers!

00:19:14.892 --> 00:19:16.328
Shields at 17%!

00:19:16.372 --> 00:19:18.548
Captain, we can't last
much longer!

00:19:24.641 --> 00:19:26.773
Captain, we are being fired upon

00:19:26.817 --> 00:19:28.906
by Klingons and Pakleds.

00:19:28.949 --> 00:19:31.300
Curious.
Shields to maximum power.

00:19:40.918 --> 00:19:43.573
The Pakleds appear
to have Klingon weaponry.

00:19:45.662 --> 00:19:47.925
Primary shields are failing.

00:19:47.968 --> 00:19:49.883
Captain, the project
I have been working on is

00:19:49.927 --> 00:19:51.624
a regenerative shield amplifier.

00:19:51.668 --> 00:19:53.147
I believe it may help.

00:19:53.191 --> 00:19:55.062
This has not been tested.

00:19:55.106 --> 00:19:56.281
If it damages the coupling,

00:19:56.325 --> 00:19:58.022
we would be left unprotected.

00:19:58.065 --> 00:19:59.893
It is logical to use it now,

00:19:59.937 --> 00:20:02.592
considering there are
no alternatives.

00:20:07.031 --> 00:20:08.859
My instinct tells me

00:20:08.902 --> 00:20:10.513
it will work.

00:20:11.644 --> 00:20:14.038
Implement the program.

00:20:16.997 --> 00:20:18.825
Yes, yes!

00:20:18.869 --> 00:20:20.740
The destruction
of two enemy ships

00:20:20.784 --> 00:20:23.047
will bring me much glory.

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:24.527
These are not our enemies.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.833
Does the high council know
of your actions?

00:20:26.877 --> 00:20:28.705
The high council lacks
foresight.

00:20:28.748 --> 00:20:31.751
They will change their minds
when the battle begins.

00:20:31.795 --> 00:20:34.188
Shields are... increasing.

00:20:34.232 --> 00:20:36.190
This is highly improbable,
Captain.

00:20:36.234 --> 00:20:37.844
They are now at 120%.

00:20:37.888 --> 00:20:40.412
Disable the Pakled ship.

00:20:46.113 --> 00:20:47.898
Target the Federation ship!

00:20:47.941 --> 00:20:49.378
Belay that order.

00:20:49.421 --> 00:20:51.815
- What?
- This is not our fight.

00:20:51.858 --> 00:20:53.991
This lunacy must end.

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:59.039
Ha! You dare challenge me?

00:20:59.083 --> 00:21:01.607
Stop the attack.

00:21:01.651 --> 00:21:03.522
- Finish them!
- No!

00:21:20.322 --> 00:21:22.454
- Stupid targ!

00:21:26.066 --> 00:21:27.546
Ah!

00:21:40.951 --> 00:21:43.606
What are your orders, Captain?

00:21:47.044 --> 00:21:49.394
Set a course for the homeworld.

00:21:49.438 --> 00:21:52.702
The council can decide
what to do with this &lt;i&gt;biHnuch.&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:55.618 --> 00:21:58.229
Captain, the Klingon
ship is retreating!

00:21:58.272 --> 00:22:00.144
Well, then,
let's give the Pakleds

00:22:00.187 --> 00:22:03.060
- a taste of their own mushfroot.
- Yes, sir!

00:22:26.866 --> 00:22:28.912
Hail the Vulcans.

00:22:28.955 --> 00:22:30.957
Thanks for the hand, Captain.

00:22:31.001 --> 00:22:33.307
For a minute there, we were
in a little over our...

00:22:33.351 --> 00:22:34.744
Do you require assistance?

00:22:34.787 --> 00:22:37.442
I think we're okay over here,
we were just...

00:22:37.486 --> 00:22:38.965
Excellent, then
with the threat neutralized,

00:22:39.009 --> 00:22:40.750
no further communication
is necessary.

00:22:41.533 --> 00:22:44.144
Well, isn't he a ton of fun?
Assess the damage.

00:22:44.188 --> 00:22:45.798
Let's begin repairs.

00:22:45.842 --> 00:22:47.409
Klingons helping Pakleds?

00:22:47.452 --> 00:22:50.324
Well, I guess now we know
how they got all those weapons.

00:22:50.368 --> 00:22:52.370
Strange how they broke off
and retreated, though.

00:22:52.414 --> 00:22:54.764
Klingons typically want
to die in battle.

00:22:54.807 --> 00:22:56.505
Honestly, I get it.

00:22:56.548 --> 00:22:58.898
It's almost like they decided

00:22:58.942 --> 00:23:01.553
- it wasn't their fight.
- Captain?

00:23:01.597 --> 00:23:03.381
We need to brief
Starfleet Command.

00:23:03.425 --> 00:23:04.861
They're gonna have
a lot to discuss

00:23:04.904 --> 00:23:06.515
with the Klingon high council.

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:15.480
We are fortunate
that your shield program worked.

00:23:15.524 --> 00:23:18.048
If you had not been
"following your instinct,"

00:23:18.091 --> 00:23:20.050
it is unlikely we would have

00:23:20.093 --> 00:23:22.356
- survived that encounter.
- I concur.

00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:24.141
However,
your inability to control

00:23:24.184 --> 00:23:25.490
your emotions is a liability.

00:23:25.534 --> 00:23:27.492
I am removing you from duty.

00:23:27.536 --> 00:23:29.451
Captain, I believe
you are making an error.

00:23:29.494 --> 00:23:32.236
Your perceived victory today
will only serve as fuel

00:23:32.279 --> 00:23:33.803
for further impulsivity.

00:23:33.846 --> 00:23:35.848
There is no place
for that on this starship.

00:23:35.892 --> 00:23:38.198
I will gather my personal items

00:23:38.242 --> 00:23:40.244
and prepare to return to Vulcan.

00:23:40.287 --> 00:23:42.855
- You will not be
returning to Vulcan.
- Curious.

00:23:42.899 --> 00:23:45.162
I am recommending you
for reassignment...

00:23:45.205 --> 00:23:47.469
to a Starfleet vessel.
Your hotheaded ways

00:23:47.512 --> 00:23:50.210
may make you better suited
to serve with humans.

00:23:50.254 --> 00:23:52.256
Captain,
I ask that you reconsider.

00:23:52.299 --> 00:23:54.519
I do not believe
this punishment is warranted.

00:23:54.563 --> 00:23:56.390
And that is exactly
the type of outburst

00:23:56.434 --> 00:23:58.131
which led to my decision.

00:23:58.175 --> 00:24:00.220
It is final.

00:24:01.265 --> 00:24:03.049
Live long and prosper.

00:24:03.093 --> 00:24:04.747
Sir.

00:24:07.358 --> 00:24:09.142
&lt;i&gt;They're all from moons!&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:09.186 --> 00:24:11.884
Look at them, probably talking
about tides and werewolves.

00:24:11.928 --> 00:24:13.538
I was so close!

00:24:13.582 --> 00:24:15.540
I know you really wanted
to have a bridge buddy,

00:24:15.584 --> 00:24:18.151
But guess what? You don't
need them-- you've got us.

00:24:18.195 --> 00:24:19.588
Next time we have
a long-haul warp,

00:24:19.631 --> 00:24:21.285
I vote we all do
something together, cool?

00:24:21.328 --> 00:24:22.547
- You know it!
- Cool!

00:24:22.591 --> 00:24:24.157
You're right. Thanks, guys.

00:24:24.201 --> 00:24:26.246
I appreciate it.

00:24:27.291 --> 00:24:29.293
E-Excuse me?

00:24:29.336 --> 00:24:30.990
Ensign Boimler, sir?

00:24:31.034 --> 00:24:33.689
- Huh? Yeah, uh, yeah, that's me.
- Well, I've been having trouble

00:24:33.732 --> 00:24:35.212
keeping up
with my duty schedule.

00:24:35.255 --> 00:24:36.605
Commander Ransom
said that you're

00:24:36.648 --> 00:24:38.520
the most organized person
on the ship.

00:24:38.563 --> 00:24:40.478
- He did?
- Yeah, he says you're great,

00:24:40.522 --> 00:24:42.698
and I should pick your brain,
if that's okay.

00:24:42.741 --> 00:24:44.090
I mean, yes! Of course!

00:24:44.134 --> 00:24:45.744
Yeah, glad to help. Sure.

00:24:45.788 --> 00:24:47.137
Oh, thank you, sir!

00:24:47.180 --> 00:24:48.921
- I really admire your work!
- Let's talk duties.

00:24:48.965 --> 00:24:51.315
Every ship in the fleet
depends on officers like us

00:24:51.358 --> 00:24:52.751
to keep them running.

00:24:52.795 --> 00:24:55.275
The bridge crew is maybe
the ones you hear about.

00:24:55.319 --> 00:24:57.103
&lt;i&gt;But trust me, the real action&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:57.147 --> 00:24:59.410
&lt;i&gt;begins on the lower decks.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:10.769 --> 00:25:15.208
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

00:26:13.049 --> 00:26:15.268
Chirp.
